## Part 3: Viva Questions & Answers

### 🔵 Architecture Questions

**Q1: Radar kya hai aur yeh kaise kaam karta hai?**
**A:** Radar ek autonomous market intelligence agent hai. Aap ek watchlist (topic) dete hain, aur system khud research questions banata hai, web se facts dhundhta hai, verify karta hai, duplicates hatake sirf nayi news briefing mein likhta hai, aur email karta hai approval ke baad. Yeh LangGraph supervisor + subgraph architecture pe chalta hai.

**Q2: Supervisor pattern kya hai? Aap ne yeh kyun use kiya?**
**A:** Supervisor ek agent hai jo har step ke baad state observe karta hai aur decide karta hai ke agla kaun sa agent chale. Hum ne yeh isliye use kiya kyunki rubric kehta hai "Wire these as subgraphs under a supervisor." Is se pipeline extensible bhi hoti hai — agar naya agent add karna ho to sirf ek aur subgraph banana hai aur supervisor mein route add karna hai.

**Q3: Subgraphs kya hain? Har agent ek subgraph kyun hai?**
**A:** Subgraph ek chhota LangGraph StateGraph hai jo sirf ek kaam karta hai. Jaise `planner_graph` sirf planning karta hai, `verifier_graph` sirf verification. Isolation milti hai — agar ek agent fail ho to baaki ke code pe asar nahi padta. LangGraph mein subgraphs ko parent graph mein add karke orchestrate kiya ja sakta hai.

**Q4: Send API kya hai? Researcher mein parallelism kaise hota hai?**
**A:** LangGraph ka `Send` function ek node ko multiple parallel instances mein chalata hai. Planner 3-5 questions deta hai, aur `route_to_researchers` har question ke liye ek `Send("researcher", {...})` bhejta hai. Matlab 5 researchers ek saath chalte hain — yeh `concurrent.futures.ThreadPoolExecutor` ki tarah hai but LangGraph managed.

**Q5: Checkpointing kaise kaam karta hai? Crash ke baad kya hota hai?**
**A:** LangGraph ka `SqliteSaver` har node transition ke baad state ko `checkpoints.sqlite` mein save karta hai. Agar server crash ho jaye to restart karne pe graph last successful step se resume hota hai. Yeh `build_graph()` mein `checkpointer=checkpointer` pass karke hota hai.

