### 🔵 Tricky / Curveball Questions

**Q26: Agar LLM bilkul galat claims de to?**
**A:** Verifier independent re-read karta hai source. Agar source uss claim ko support nahi karta to verdict "rejected" hota hai aur claim briefing mein nahi aata. Agar confidence < 0.5 ho to bhi reject hota hai. Yeh fail-closed design hai.

**Q27: Ek run beach mein crash ho jaye to?**
**A:** LangGraph checkpoints har step ke baad. Restart karne pe last successful step se resume hota hai. Briefing phir se nahi likhi jaati — purana state restore hota hai.

**Q28: Cost kitna aata hai per run?**
**A:** ~5 questions × 3 results = 15 researcher LLM calls + ~15 verifier batch calls + 1 writer call = ~31 LLM calls max. DuckDuckGo free hai. Ollama se local cost = $0. Groq free tier mein aa sakta hai (100k tokens/day limit).

**Q29: Duplicate news kaise filter hoti hai?**
**A:** ChromaDB mein har claim ka embedding store hota hai. Naye findings aane pe `filter_new_findings()` check karta hai ke koi purane claim se ≥0.75 cosine similar hai. Agar hai to woh claim "not new" mark hota hai aur briefing mein nahi aata.

**Q30: Email kaise bhejta hai? Gmail kyun?**
**A:** `smtplib.SMTP_SSL` se Gmail ke SMTP server (`smtp.gmail.com:465`) pe connect hota hai. `GMAIL_APP_PASSWORD` se login — yeh Gmail ka security feature hai jo bina actual password ke access deta hai. Default recipient = sender (self-email). Production mein Telegram/Slack webhook bhi ho sakta hai.

